> Compare true and learned densities on the same grid and colour scale

All 16,384 grid centers lie in [-4,4]² at spacing 1/16. Rows run from high y
to low y in the saved source arrays. The plot explicitly reverses that storage
axis to draw physical y upward. Both panels use the same native terrain palette
and density range 0..0.20, with square cells and equal coordinate units. The
finite window is a visualization; it does not claim the density integrates to
one within this box. The exact global normalization follows the invertible map
and its Gaussian base, checked separately below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/glow_density.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> data;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/grid.npz"))data[k]=x;
 std::vector<double> axis;for(int i=0;i<128;++i)axis.push_back((i+.5)/16-4);
 auto panel=[&](const char* key,const char* title){auto p=n::exp(data.at(key)).to_vector<double>();
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> z(128,std::vector<double>(128));
  for(int x=0;x<128;++x)for(int y=0;y<128;++y)z[x][y]=p[(127-y)*128+x];
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.image(axis,axis,z,dm::graphics::terrain_colors(32),0,.20)
  .margins(72,22,54,64).x_limits(-4,4).y_limits(-4,4).x_label("x0").y_label("x1").title(title);return plot;};
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(panel("true_log_probability","Analytic banana PDF"))
 .add(panel("model_log_probability","Final Glow PDF")).size(1100,574).fit_panels()
 .save_svg("build/glow_density.svg");
}
