> Retain all inverse samples and all transformed held-out points

The first scatter overlays every generated point with every held-out point in
observation coordinates. The next compares transformed held-out points with
all Gaussian-prior draws in latent coordinates. Both retain points beyond the
source's smaller plotting window, using equal coordinate scales. They are
qualitative distribution views, not a two-sample test or proof of a good fit.

