> Show the input-dependent volume factors on both paths

These panels retain each analytic determinant and its actual-Jacobian check.
Forward points use observed x0; inverse points use supplied Gaussian z0.
The other coordinate also affects the map, so a vertical spread at the same
horizontal coordinate is expected. These are point clouds, not single-variable
functions or paired forward/inverse observations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/glow_volume.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> data,out,samples,v;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/data.npz"))data[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/outputs.npz"))out[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/samples.npz"))samples[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/plot_values.npz"))v[k]=x;
 auto panel=[&](const n::Tensor& points,const n::Tensor& analytic,const n::Tensor& actual,const char* title,const char* xlabel){
  auto x=n::select(points,1,0).to_vector<double>();auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points(x,analytic.to_vector<double>(),"Analytic logdet",{37,99,235},3)
  .points(x,actual.to_vector<double>(),"Actual Jacobian",{234,88,12},1)
  .margins(72,22,54,64).y_limits(-1.3,1.6).x_label(xlabel).y_label("Log absolute determinant, nats").title(title);return p;};
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2)
 .add(panel(data.at("test_points"),out.at("forward_logdet"),v.at("actual_logdet"),"Forward: all128 test rows","Observed x0"))
 .add(panel(samples.at("prior"),samples.at("inverse_logdet"),v.at("inverse_actual_logdet"),"Inverse: all1024 prior rows","Supplied latent z0"))
 .size(1100,500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/glow_volume.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/glow_volume.svg)
// result_end

\caption(All 128 forward and 1,024 inverse log determinants are retained twice, once from the analytic path and once from the actual Jacobian. Their input dependence is visible; the next plot resolves their small Float32 disagreement.)
\alttext(Two scatter panels show variable forward and inverse log determinants. Small orange actual-Jacobian points coincide with larger blue analytic points for every row.)

> Check actual forward and inverse determinants along their own paths

Reverse-mode differentiation of each output coordinate yields two actual
Jacobian rows. Their positive determinant agrees with the per-row analytic
logdet on all 128 held-out points and all 1,024 inverse samples. The forward
logdet ranges from −.869011223 to .505490065; it is not a global constant.
The inverse logdet is computed from its supplied latent coordinates along the
reversed affine path. The following residual plot retains all 1,152 values,
subtracts the matching analytic value for each row and scales by 1e7 to reveal
Float32 errors. The two row indices refer to different pools, not paired points.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/glow_jacobians.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> v,o,samples;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/plot_values.npz"))v[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/outputs.npz"))o[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/glow_density/samples.npz"))samples[k]=x;
 auto a=(v.at("actual_logdet")-n::cast(o.at("forward_logdet"),n::DType::Float64))*1e7,b=(v.at("inverse_actual_logdet")-n::cast(samples.at("inverse_logdet"),n::DType::Float64))*1e7;
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(n::arange(0,128).to_vector<double>(),a.to_vector<double>(),"Forward, all128 test rows",{37,99,235},3)
 .points(n::arange(0,1024).to_vector<double>(),b.to_vector<double>(),"Inverse, all1024 prior rows",{234,88,12},2)
 .y_limits(-5,7).x_label("Row index in its own pool").y_label("(Actual - analytic logdet) x 1e7")
 .title("Actual Jacobians match each per-point log determinant")
 .save_svg("build/glow_jacobians.svg");
}
```
